eturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":2199.00,\"sku\":\"MDYQ4LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{\"@type\":\"OfferShippingDetails\",\"shippingRate\":{\"@type\":\"MonetaryAmount\",\"value\":0,\"currency\":\"USD\"}},\"hasMerchantReturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":2799.00,\"sku\":\"ME8K4LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{\"@type\":\"OfferShippingDetails\",\"shippingRate\":{\"@type\":\"MonetaryAmount\",\"value\":0,\"currency\":\"USD\"}},\"hasMerchantReturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":2699.00,\"sku\":\"MDYV4LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":"},{"title":"iPad Air (1st generation)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Air_(1st_generation)","snippet":"iPad Air (1st generation)\nDiscontinued 64 GB & 128 GB: October 16, 2014 16 GB & 32 GB: March 21, 2016\nSystem on a chip Apple A7 with 64-bit architecture and Apple M7 motion co-processor\nMemory 1 GB LPDDR3 RAM [ 2 ]\nStorage 16, 32, 64, 128 GB [ a ] flash memory\nDisplay 9.7 inches (250 mm) 2,048 × 1,536 px color IPS dis…","date":"2026-08-09T00:30:12.000Z","content":"iPad Air (1st generation)\nDiscontinued 64 GB & 128 GB: October 16, 2014 16 GB & 32 GB: March 21, 2016\nSystem on a chip Apple A7 with 64-bit architecture and Apple M7 motion co-processor\nMemory 1 GB LPDDR3 RAM [ 2 ]\nStorage 16, 32, 64, 128 GB [ a ] flash memory\nDisplay 9.7 inches (250 mm) 2,048 × 1,536 px color IPS display , [ 3 ] (264 ppi ) with a 4:3 aspect ratio, oleophobic coating\nInput Multi-touch screen , headset controls , M7 motion co-processor, proximity and ambient light sensors, 3-axis accelerometer , 3-axis gyroscope , digital compass , dual microphone\nCamera Front : 1.2 MP, 720p HD Rear : OmniVision Technologies OV5650 5.0 MP AF, iSight with Five Element Lens, Hybrid IR filter , video stabilisation, face detection, HDR, ƒ/2.4 aperture\nConnectivity Wi-Fi and Wi-Fi + Cellular: Wi-Fi 802.11 a / b / g / n at 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz and MIMO Bluetooth 4.0 Wi-Fi + Cellular: GPS & GLONASS GSM UMTS / HSDPA 850, 1700, 1900, 2100 MHz GSM / EDGE 850, 900, 1800, 1900 MHz CDMA CDMA / EV-DO Rev. A and B. 800, 1900 MHz LTE Multiple bands A1475 : 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 25, 26; A1476 : 1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 18, 19, 20 and TD-LTE 38, 39, 40\nPower Built-in rechargeable Li-Po battery 8,827 mAh 3.73 V 32.9 W⋅h (118 kJ) [ 4 ]\nOnline services App Store , iTunes Store , iBookstore , iCloud , Game Center\nDimensions 240 mm (9.4 in) (h) 169.5 mm (6.67 in) (w) 7.5 mm (0.30 in) (d)\nWeight Wi-Fi: 469 g (1.034 lb) Wi-Fi + Cellular: 478 g (1.054 lb)\nPredecessor iPad (4th generation)\nWebsite Apple - iPad Air at the Wayback Machine (archived December 14, 2013)","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Pro (9.7-inch) Prices - CNET","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20160414145719/http:/www.cnet.com/products/apple-ipad-pro-9-7-inch/prices","snippet":"Apple iPad Pro (9.7-inch)\n$599.00\nMSRP: $599.00\n$599.00\nMSRP: $599.00","date":"2026-06-11T12:03:53.000Z","domain":"web.archive.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"ipad-pro","url":"https://thairesidents.com/lifestyle/bma-surveys-sale-new-year-hampers/attachment/ipad-pro/","snippet":"","date":"2026-08-19T00:01:16.000Z","domain":"thairesidents.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Pro (9.7-inch) Prices - CNET","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20160412211114/http:/www.cnet.com/products/apple-ipad-pro-9-7-inch/prices","snippet":"Apple iPad Pro (9.7-inch)\n$599.00\nMSRP: $599.00\n$599.00\nMSRP: $599.00","date":"2026-06-11T13:13:13.000Z","domain":"web.archive.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Want iPad Pro 🥵😩","url":"https://buymeacoffee.com/131377/want-ipad-pro","snippet":"","date":"2026-08-16T11:47:08.000Z","domain":"buymeacoffee.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"How much does the newest ipad pro cost","url":"https://magasoftsfnzlbp.netlify.app/how-much-does-the-newest-ipad-pro-cost-625","snippet":"The iPad, iPad 2 or iPad Air will cost $249. The iPad 3, iPad 4, iPad Mini 3, iPad Mini 4 and iPad Air 2 screen replacements cost $299. The 9.7-inch iPad Pro has a $379 price tag for the screen replacement and the 12.9-inch iPad Pro costs $599. How to pick the best iPad Pro storage option for you Nov 02, 2018 · The 25…","date":"2026-07-18T11:14:38.000Z","content":"The iPad, iPad 2 or iPad Air will cost $249. The iPad 3, iPad 4, iPad Mini 3, iPad Mini 4 and iPad Air 2 screen replacements cost $299. The 9.7-inch iPad Pro has a $379 price tag for the screen replacement and the 12.9-inch iPad Pro costs $599. How to pick the best iPad Pro storage option for you Nov 02, 2018 · The 256GB iPad Pro is the right choice for almost everyone. It’s the best value, and costs just $150 more than there base model, for four times the capacity. Heres why it’s right for you. How much extra will connecting my iPad Pro cost? - AT&T Re: How much extra will connecting my iPad Pro cost? @dbcallsr If you want to connect it to a postpaid plan, the tablet line fee depends on which unlimited plan ... AppleCare+ for New iPad Pro Models Priced at $130, Out-of","domain":"magasoftsfnzlbp.netlify.app","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Air","url":"https://www.gsmarena.com/apple_ipad_air-5797.php","snippet":"Versions: Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi + Cellular (3G/LTE); Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi, w/o GPS)\n2G bands GSM 850 / 900 / 1800 / 1900\n3G bands HSDPA 850 / 900 / 1700(AWS) / 1900 / 2100\n4G bands 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 25, 26\nSpeed HSPA 42.2/5.76 Mbps, LTE Cat3 100/50 Mbps, EV-DO Rev.A 3.1 Mbps - cellular mod…","date":"2026-08-08T04:01:10.000Z","content":"Versions: Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi + Cellular (3G/LTE); Apple iPad Air Wi-Fi (Wi-Fi, w/o GPS)\n2G bands GSM 850 / 900 / 1800 / 1900\n3G bands HSDPA 850 / 900 / 1700(AWS) / 1900 / 2100\n4G bands 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 25, 26\nSpeed HSPA 42.2/5.76 Mbps, LTE Cat3 100/50 Mbps, EV-DO Rev.A 3.1 Mbps - cellular model only\nLaunch Announced 2013, October 22. Released 2013, November 01\nBody Dimensions 240 x 169.5 x 7.5 mm (9.45 x 6.67 x 0.30 in)","domain":"gsmarena.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Það er að koma verslunarmannahelgi svo það verður lokað 31 júlí til 3. ágúst.","url":"https://reykjavikfoto.is/vefverslun/myndavelar/videovelar/atvinnuvelar/sigma-fp-m-45mm-f-28/","snippet":"12%\nOriginal price was: 399.990 kr..\nCurrent price is: 351.991 kr..\n12%\nOriginal price was: 279.990 kr..\nCurrent price is: 246.391 kr..\nMacBook Pro 14\" M5 Pro 1TB / 24GB - Fartölva","date":"2026-08-04T13:14:22.000Z","domain":"reykjavikfoto.is","engines":["web"]},{"title":"2021 Apple iPad Pro: Should You Upgrade?","url":"https://www.pcmag.com/news/2021-apple-ipad-pro-should-you-upgrade","snippet":"Rumors about a price bump for the iPad Pro were partially true. The cheapest, 11-inch iPad Pro still clocks in at $799, but the base, 12.9-inch model is now $100 more expensive at $1,099. For 5G connectivity, prices start at $999 and go up from there. If you want the top-of-the line, 11-inch iPad Pro Wi-Fi + 5G Cellul…","date":"2026-09-23T15:00:16.000Z","content":"Rumors about a price bump for the iPad Pro were partially true. The cheapest, 11-inch iPad Pro still clocks in at $799, but the base, 12.9-inch model is now $100 more expensive at $1,099. For 5G connectivity, prices start at $999 and go up from there. If you want the top-of-the line, 11-inch iPad Pro Wi-Fi + 5G Cellular, expect to spend $2,099. For the 12.9-inch model, it's $2,399.\nPre-order a new iPad Pro beginning Friday, April 30. They arrive in the second half of May.","domain":"pcmag.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"2021 iPad Pro is available now, just not from Apple.com","url":"https://www.cultofmac.com/news/2021-ipad-pro-12-9-available-now-just-not-from-apple-com","snippet":"The online Apple Store might not be the best place to buy the 12.9-inch iPad Pro. Place an order for 2021’s hottest tablet on Apple.com on Wednesday and you could wait a month or more to have it shipped to you. But other stores have the device in stock now.\nFor many, the online Apple Store is the default place to buy…","date":"2021-06-16T23:26:15.000Z","content":"The online Apple Store might not be the best place to buy the 12.9-inch iPad Pro. Place an order for 2021’s hottest tablet on Apple.com on Wednesday and you could wait a month or more to have it shipped to you. But other stores have the device in stock now.\nFor many, the online Apple Store is the default place to buy an iPad. But a base model 12.9-inch iPad Pro with 8GB of RAM and 128GB of storage ordered June 16 won’t be delivered until sometime between July 16 and July 30 — a month away. And that doesn’t change for other configurations of the 12.9-inch model.\nThe situation is different with brick-and-mortar Apple stores. The company seems to be scattering its available stock of 2021 iPad Pro units to its retail locations. A check of random cities around the U.S. found the base model in some of these, but certainly not all.\nFor example, an Apple Store in Dallas has the 12.9-inch tablet in stock, but the next nearest option is in Austin. There are none of the base model in stock in Atlanta or Portand. But those who live in Los Angeles have multiple locations to choose from.\nNote that the long wait times don’t apply to the latest 11-inch iPad Pro. Apple can ship that before the end of June. But ths smaller version doesn’t have a mini-LED display, which is causing much of the delay in the 12.9-inch model.","domain":"cultofmac.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"iPads Pro Archives - Techstreet","url":"http://ec2-54-179-16-94.ap-southeast-1.compute.amazonaws.com/product-category/ipads/ipads-pro?stock_status=onbackorder","snippet":"No products were found matching your selection.\nStart typing to see products you are looking for.\nMac Mini iMac iPads iPads Pro iPad Air iPad iPad mini iPhone iPhone 17 Pro iPhone 17 Pro Max iPhone Air","date":"2026-07-11T22:09:35.000Z","domain":"ec2-54-179-16-94.ap-southeast-1.compute.amazonaws.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"IPad Pro","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Pro","snippet":"The iPad Pro is a series of tablet computers, positioned as the premium line of Apple's iPad brand. Models run i Pad OS, a tablet-optimized fork of the","date":"2026-10-03T21:44:38Z","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple iPad Pro (9.7-inch) Prices - CNET","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20160413010606/http:/www.cnet.com/products/apple-ipad-pro-9-7-inch/prices","snippet":"Apple iPad Pro (9.7-inch)\n$599.00\nMSRP: $599.00\n$599.00\nMSRP: $599.00","date":"2026-06-11T13:54:29.000Z","domain":"web.archive.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"IPad","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad","snippet":"Since then, the iPad product line has been expanded to include the smaller iPad Mini, the lighter and thinner iPad Air, and the flagship iPad Pro models.","date":"2026-10-08T19:04:06Z","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple M4","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_M4","snippet":"signal processor (DSP). The M4 SoC was introduced in May 2024 for the iPad Pro (7th generation), and is the fourth generation of the M series Apple silicon","date":"2026-09-22T20:46:39Z","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"Apple silicon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_silicon","snippet":"including Mac, i Phone, iPad , Apple TV, Apple Watch, AirPods, AirTag, HomePod, and Apple Vision Pro . The first Apple-designed SoC was the Apple A4, introduced","date":"2026-10-06T03:50:54Z","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]}],"images":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Pro","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Wikipedia_on_iPad_Pro.jpg/330px-Wikipedia_on_iPad_Pro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","title":"IPad Pro","source":"en.wikipedia.org","license":"source","credit":"Wikipedia"},{"url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/8569941@N04/27748137870","thumb":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/564b5b84-bb31-4655-b5ad-4c9fdc4dd9a7/thumb/","title":"My Desk 2016","source":"flickr.com","license":"open","credit":"saebaryo · CC BY-ND 2.0 · flickr"},{"url":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/79016591@N07/28606886073","thumb":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/3c092471-3a00-42b9-82e7-ebf1c0cef834/thumb/","title":"Testing the Pro and Pencil","source":"flickr.com","license":"open","credit":"aehdeschaine · CC BY-ND 2.0 · flickr"}],"knowledge":{"title":"IPad Pro","extract":"The iPad Pro is a series of tablet computers, positioned as the premium line of Apple's iPad brand. Models run iPadOS, a tablet-optimized fork of the iOS operating system. Early models were distinguished from other iPads by their ability to use the Apple Pencil stylus and their larger screen size. As other iPads have gained these features over time, the latest eighth-generation iPad Pro is notable among other features for its powerful processor and being the thinnest Apple product ever released.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Pro","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Wikipedia_on_iPad_Pro.jpg/330px-Wikipedia_on_iPad_Pro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","description":"Line of Apple tablet computers (2015–present)"},"discussions":[{"title":"Rate my business plan: Porting a classic to the iPad","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1989740","points":2,"comments":1,"date":"2010-12-09T23:26:53Z"},{"title":"Can I make graphics-intensive IpadOS apps without a mac?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=29944450","points":1,"comments":1,"date":"2022-01-15T07:26:31Z"},{"title":"Ask HN: Apple filed to patent an app concept that I released a year ago. ","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=3760237","points":35,"comments":9,"date":"2012-03-27T05:54:42Z"},{"title":"Ask HN: Is Linux the best way to get my elderly parents new cheapo Dell to work?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=22232025","points":2,"comments":9,"date":"2020-02-04T03:18:11Z"},{"title":"Ask HN: Apple North Carolina Data Center","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1780503","points":1,"comments":1,"date":"2010-10-11T17:49:58Z"},{"title":"Ask HN: Do you feel bad when devices aren't utilized to the extreme?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=33832448","points":71,"comments":126,"date":"2022-12-02T16:14:11Z"}],"engines":[{"name":"web","ok":false,"count":0,"ms":0,"error":"skipped"},{"name":"web","ok":true,"count":20,"ms":4001},{"name":"web","ok":true,"count":5,"ms":283}]}

